from write_records import add,N
from araw_dependencies import R1,R2

def claims(rows):return '\n'.join(f'C{i}. {r[0]} — OPEN implementation hypothesis; {r[5]} in the separate ARAW dependency.' for i,r in enumerate(rows,1))

def gu(n,title,goal,start,rows,dep,journey,chains,questions,cmp,change):
 body=f'''Interpretation: understand the task’s stated goal, not reverse-engineer an unseen person’s latent objective. Original goal captured from the supplied assignment, verbatim: “{goal}.” The supplied goal is the working premise; it is not rejected or replaced by an easier endpoint.

Context: normal time pressure; medium stakes for the integrity of this inquiry; expertise mixed by domain; local writing and case comparison reversible; human relational actions not performed; complexity COMPOUND. Lead goal is a faithful, useful local investigation. Other subgoals include breadth, efficient uptake, preserved autonomy, and distinct human-effect evaluation. Source loading enables execution; execution enables a scoped transfer test; neither entails a human change. Personal ultimate reasons remain unknown.

Clarification/substitution check: splitting the goal into observable targets preserves its kinds of success. Renaming it “make a plan,” “perform more tasks,” or “change only beliefs” would change success and is not adopted. Completing available local work while recording unavailable stages does not mark the whole goal complete. No nontrivial substituted goal is selected.

CLOSED as supplied task premises: this goal is requested in the assignment; original procedures are to be used; human effects must not be fabricated; forced action is not the sole endpoint. These are accepted instructions, not empirical proof of a person’s entire value hierarchy.

OPEN claims parsed and tested:

{claims(rows)}

→ /araw 8x invoked separately: {dep}.md and {dep}.json. That original execution contains eighteen exact claims, eighty-five findings, ten cruxes, twelve valid linked recursive edges on the deepest branch, and two actual generated input/output tests. The last compatible-boundary objection is explicitly failed and excluded from depth. All root countercases bear on the exact claim; a favorable scoped case does not rescue a rejected universal. These tests establish their particular output mappings, not the general effectiveness of this inquiry for people.

Goal journey structure:

{journey}

Domains: personal growth in the task sense, creative exploration, professional/social reasoning, and epistemic representation. No private health or biographical domain is imported.

→ /ve invoked on the unelicited intrinsic-goal component; exact original and receipt are already retained. Concrete candidate chains:

{chains}

Circularity check: a task terminus can be accepted because the supplied request values it; that is not a collected human answer to why it matters. Additional intrinsic goals cannot be declared exhausted because no respondent said there are none. Conflict check preserves the specified competing termini. The elicitation stage therefore remains partial, with no invented interview answers.

Questions generated and prioritized, not used as needless blockers to the already authorized work:

{questions}

→ /cmp invoked for the concrete local options below. The cmp source specifies no numerical 8x table; the complete impression, required-criterion elimination, tier comparison, divergence check and recommendation are supplied.

{cmp}

Routing: /ve is the next required live elicitation only if a later choice depends on a personal intrinsic priority not supplied here. /cmp resolves the available reversible implementation choice. This is a goal request, not a new problem statement requiring /pbi. A complete personally grounded goal journey is not ready while its termini are unelicited, so /gjs and its /emv branch are not falsely marked executed. Their loaded originals remain available; they are not substituted for the present missing answers.

Subsequent application: the two actual transformed inputs/outputs in the separate ARAW execution are used as the local classification examples for this goal record. No participant is contacted and no new goal is accepted on their behalf.

Certificate: the authorization premises stay fixed; OPEN means implementation claims have alternatives, not that the user’s stated want is disregarded. The ARAW countercases reject particular sufficiency claims; the resulting local choice does not certify a human or whole-program outcome.'''
 add('gu',n,title,'Clarify the goal’s actual commitments and dependencies while preserving its full scope.',start,body,change,'The goal record can support bounded next work and preserve missing human inputs without substituting a smaller success criterion.','UNRESOLVED','Content distinguishes accepted authorization, tested implementation hypotheses, unelicited personal termini and pending human stages. Organization links exact source, separate ARAW registry, value chains and option comparison; no universal completion claim follows.','Resolve a truly action-changing intrinsic priority when a real choice requires it; test a new target class; compare the selected local approach against an actual supplied human response.',N+' All standard GU operations are supplied; required ARAW dependency meets its explicit 8x floors. VE remains partial for missing live answers; conditional routing is stated explicitly.')

gu(1,'Broad mind change: a goal with several kinds of success','autonomous beneficial efficient broad mind change','The task has clear operational commitments, but its relationship to the user’s ultimate personal values remains underdetermined; I can work locally without pretending those values are elicited.',R1,'dependency-gu-1-araw',
'''CURRENT STATE: source-specific applications can be produced; many human outcomes are unavailable.
DESIRED STATE: diverse beneficial changes with inspectable consequences and efficient later uptake.
IMMEDIATE GOAL: test the assigned operations on different targets and preserve actual results.
SERVES: broader beneficial inquiry, explicitly supplied; personal significance beyond that UNKNOWN.
INTRINSIC GOAL: personal termini UNKNOWN; task values include truth, breadth, autonomy and usefulness.
WHY NOW: continuation assigned; personal trigger UNKNOWN.
SUCCESS CRITERIA: faithful products, distinct later use for KEEP, no invented human change, transparent partials.
CONSTRAINTS: assigned scope, original floors, no unauthorized human interaction, no easier goal substitution.''',
'''1. Exact original → faithful operation → honoring requested method → task fidelity.
2. Diverse targets → wider changes available → broad inquiry → task breadth.
3. Actual later use → demonstrated consequence → beneficial change → task usefulness.
4. Failed cases retained → avoid false success → credible selection → truthfulness.
5. Interesting thread followed → new attention relation → exploration for its own sake → intrinsic-interest candidate.
6. Compact retained distinctions → less repeated work → more available inquiry effort → efficiency.
7. Optional contribution preserved → choice remains real → agency → autonomy candidate.
8. Actual reciprocal response distinguished → no fabricated relationship effect → honest joint inquiry → reciprocity candidate.
Conflicts: efficiency/breadth; curiosity/immediate benefit; scope/available evidence; own control/reciprocal outcomes.''',
'''HIGH: Which later choice would reverse under a different personal priority? No current local source execution depends on that answer.
HIGH: What actual response would establish a human change? Missing recipient/participant evidence remains a specific dependency.
MEDIUM: Which target class has received insufficient coverage? Answer changes next allocation, not the goal.
LOW: Which layout is preferred for a personal summary? Deferred because the current source products remain useful under either presentation.''',
'''Options: A continue diverse local applications with partial-stage ledger; B stop all work pending personal value interview; C write only motivational action tips. Initial impression A, medium confidence.
Required criteria: preserve broad goal; execute originals; no false human outcomes. A passes all three; B preserves scope but fails current autonomous continuation when available work exists; C fails original operations and scope. Under a genuine blocking personal decision B could become appropriate; C would require a different authorized task.
Important tiers: A clearly better than B on completed available work; A equivalent on honesty if both accurately label missing stages; A better than C on fidelity, while C is shorter but eliminated. Nice-to-have: one compact index.
Overall A. Impression and analysis agree; no hidden criterion is needed. Risk: local work is mistaken for full human completion, addressed by the explicit ledger. Reversibility: local artifact organization can be changed without changing the underlying goal.''',
'The broad goal remains intact; the available local route is chosen with human and personal-value dependencies explicit. These distinctions mostly reuse established keeps, so no new KEEP is assigned.')

gu(2,'Reciprocal change without manufacturing a relationship','changes in motivation, intrinsic interest, goals, role, value conflict, attention, trust, social interpretation and reciprocal interaction','Several target classes are ready for constructed analysis, but a reciprocal relationship outcome cannot be produced by one-sided generated text alone.',R2,'dependency-gu-2-araw',
'''CURRENT STATE: the corpus contains constructed social cases and generated response designs; real participant responses are absent.
DESIRED STATE: beneficial changes across all named targets, including actual reciprocal interaction when evidence exists.
IMMEDIATE GOAL: distinguish what can be transformed now from what requires another actor.
SERVES: the supplied broad mind-change program; no hidden personal motive is inferred.
INTRINSIC GOAL: reciprocity, curiosity, agency and accurate understanding are task-linked candidates, personally unelicited.
WHY NOW: assigned continuation across social/motivational targets; personal trigger UNKNOWN.
SUCCESS CRITERIA: accurate local inference changes plus honest separation from unobserved social outcomes.
CONSTRAINTS: no forced participation, no fictional consent, preserve scope and originals.''',
'''1. More precise social question → discriminating response opportunity → understanding → epistemic connection candidate.
2. Faithful objection summary → real disagreement retained → autonomy in judgment → agency candidate.
3. Correctly scoped assent → no invented commitment → reliable coordination → integrity candidate.
4. Voluntary invitation → possible response → reciprocal inquiry → connection candidate.
5. Interesting shared object → new questions → exploration → intrinsic-interest candidate.
6. Honest trust dimension → appropriate reliance → less avoidable task mismatch → usefulness.
7. Distinct role authority → correct handoff → cooperative work → shared creation candidate.
8. Preserved decline option → contribution freely chosen → authentic participation → agency candidate.
Conflicts: shared activity/different interests; speed/permission; candor/ease; curiosity/commitment.''',
'''HIGH: Did the other person actually receive and accept the specific proposal? This determines an agreement claim.
HIGH: What exact condition does the objection concern—fact, meaning, priority or permission? This changes the response.
MEDIUM: Which role holds the decision or disclosure authority? This changes permissible next acts.
MEDIUM: Would the person prefer no further discussion? A real response could terminate the invitation branch.
LOW: Which conversational style is preferred? Useful only after the substantive issue is clear.''',
'''Options: A produce a source-specific perspective/permission analysis with generated drafts and pending outcomes; B simulate a full conversation and count agreement; C abandon all social targets because real actors are absent. Initial impression A, high confidence on honesty but limited on benefit.
Required: preserve social targets; avoid invented response; execute available original operations. A passes; B fails evidence; C drops available target work. B could be used as explicitly labeled fiction, but not as a completed social result. C is justified only for unavailable stages, not every analysis.
Important tiers: A is clearly better on present inspectable work; A retains uncertainty like C without deleting all possibilities; A keeps actual reciprocity as an uncompleted endpoint. Nice-to-have is a reusable draft conditional on real input.
Overall A; impression and criteria agree. Risk: a reader overreads vivid narratives, so their constructed status and confidence remain adjacent. Reversible choice: the model is updated when an actual response arrives.''',
'The goal model preserves reciprocal interaction as a real target while keeping one-sided analyses and drafts explicitly partial. No human relationship change or additional distinct KEEP is established.')
